# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: dxf-angle-units-hatch-viewport-tables -- the DXF codec still copies the degree angles of HATCH, VIEWPORT, table records and header variables unconverted
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: dxf-file-angle-units
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-22

* Symptom

dxf-file-angle-units (2.3.31) converts the entity angles of ARC, TEXT,
ATTRIB, ATTDEF, SHAPE, MTEXT, INSERT, DIMENSION and VERTEX between the
file's degrees and entget's radians. Still copied unconverted, per the DXF
reference:

- HATCH: 52 (pattern angle), 53 (pattern line angle), and the boundary
  path's ARC / ELLIPSE edges' 50/51 (start / end angle) -- nested in the
  boundary data, so the first-occurrence rule of *DXF-DEGREE-GROUPS* does
  not fit them;
- VIEWPORT 51 (twist angle);
- table records: VPORT 50/51 (snap rotation, view twist), VIEW 50, UCS
  /dimstyle angles as applicable;
- header variables holding angles ($ANGBASE, $SNAPANG, ...) -- check the
  unit of each against the reference and a vendor file.

* To do

Check each against the DXF reference and a vendor-written DXF (the
dxf-file-angle-units ticket's vendor check can cover these too), then
extend the codec: a structured walk for HATCH boundary edges, table-record
and header tables alongside *DXF-DEGREE-GROUPS*.
